-- ============================================================================
-- F1: § 67 says "dyrke Gud" — worship GOD.
--
-- The text: "at forene sig i samfund for at dyrke GUD"
-- Singular. Capitalized. This is a MONOTHEISTIC formulation.
--
-- Does § 67 protect:
--   - Polytheism (multiple gods)? Text says "Gud", not "guder"
--   - Buddhism (no personal god)? "Dyrke Gud" doesn't cover meditation
--   - Atheist communities? They explicitly don't worship God
--   - Satanism? Is Satan "Gud"?
--
-- Our encoding says "dyrke Gud efter overbevisning" without noting
-- that the text frames religious freedom through a monotheistic lens.
-- The 1849/1953 drafters assumed religion = worshipping God.
--
-- Modern interpretation extends this, but the TEXT is limited.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F1: § 67 'dyrke Gud' — monotheistic formulation ---")
@ print("Text: 'at forene sig i samfund for at dyrke GUD'")
@ print("'Gud' — singular, capitalized. Monotheistic framing.")
@ print("")
@ print("Constitutionally protected (by text):")
@ print("  Christianity, Judaism, Islam: JA (worship God)")
@ print("  Hinduism (many gods): ? ('Gud' is singular)")
@ print("  Buddhism (no god): ? ('dyrke Gud' doesn't cover meditation)")
@ print("  Atheist communities: NEJ ('dyrke Gud' is the opposite)")
@ print("  Satanism: ? (Is the Devil 'Gud'?)")
@ print("")
@ print("Our encoding: doesn't note the monotheistic limitation")
@ print("Severity: STRUKTUREL — the text is narrower than we encoded")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F2: § 69 says "afvigende" — DEVIATING.
--
-- The text: "De fra folkekirken AFVIGENDE trossamfund"
-- Not "andre" (other). Not "forskellige" (different). AFVIGENDE (deviating).
--
-- The Folkekirke is the NORM. Everything else is a DEVIATION.
-- This is normative language in a chapter about non-discrimination.
-- The very paragraph that regulates non-Folkekirke denominations
-- describes them as "deviating" from the standard.
--
-- § 70 then says "ingen kan... berøves... rettigheder" based on creed.
-- But § 69 linguistically frames non-Folkekirke religions as deviant.
--
-- Our encoding notes the § 66 vs § 69 asymmetry (forfatning vs forhold)
-- but doesn't capture this loaded terminology.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F2: § 69 'afvigende' — normative framing ---")
@ print("Text: 'De fra folkekirken AFVIGENDE trossamfund'")
@ print("Not 'andre' (other). Not 'forskellige' (different).")
@ print("AFVIGENDE — deviating. The Folkekirke is the norm.")
@ print("")
@ print("In a chapter about religious non-discrimination,")
@ print("the constitution linguistically frames all non-Folkekirke")
@ print("religions as DEVIATIONS from the standard.")
@ print("Our encoding notes the asymmetry but not this loaded language.")
@ print("Severity: STRUKTUREL — captures the constitutional worldview")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F3: § 71 stk. 1 says "ingen DANSK BORGER" — only DANISH CITIZENS.
--
-- Text: "Ingen DANSK BORGER kan på grund af sin politiske eller
--  religiøse overbevisning eller sin afstamning underkastes
--  nogen form for frihedsberøvelse."
--
-- Compare:
--   § 70: "Ingen" (nobody — universal)
--   § 71: "Ingen DANSK BORGER" (no Danish citizen — restricted)
--   § 77: "Enhver" (everyone — universal)
--
-- The Bill of Rights SWITCHES between universal and citizen-specific:
--   Universal: §§ 70, 77 (equality, free speech)
--   Citizen-specific: § 71 (personal liberty)
--
-- This means: a non-citizen in Denmark has free speech (§ 77)
-- but NOT the same personal liberty protections (§ 71 stk. 1).
--
-- Our encoding says "personlig_frihed_ukraenkelig" without the
-- citizen-specific scope. This is a significant fidelity gap.
-- ============================================================================

> paragraf_subjekt_70() -> Subjekt { Ingen }
> paragraf_subjekt_71() -> Subjekt { DanskBorger }
> paragraf_subjekt_77() -> Subjekt { Enhver }
> paragraf_subjekt_78() -> Subjekt { Borgerne }

@ print("--- F3: § 71 'ingen DANSK BORGER' — citizen-specific scope ---")
@ print("Text: 'Ingen DANSK BORGER kan...'")
@ print("")
@ print("Subject scope across the Bill of Rights:")
@ print("  § 70: 'Ingen' (nobody — " + show(paragraf_subjekt_70()) + ")")
@ print("  § 71: 'Ingen DANSK BORGER' (" + show(paragraf_subjekt_71()) + ")")
@ print("  § 77: 'Enhver' (everyone — " + show(paragraf_subjekt_77()) + ")")
@ print("  § 78: 'Borgerne' (the citizens — " + show(paragraf_subjekt_78()) + ")")
@ print("")
@ print("The constitution SWITCHES between universal and citizen-specific!")
@ print("Our encoding treats § 71 as universal. Text says DANISH CITIZENS.")
@ print("Severity: MENINGSAENDRENDE — changes WHO is protected")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F4: § 71 stk. 6 EXPLICITLY exempts immigration detention.
--
-- Text: "en frihedsberøvelse, der ikke er besluttet af en
--  dømmende myndighed, og som IKKE har hjemmel i lovgivningen
--  om UDLÆNDINGE"
--
-- This says: non-criminal detention must be judicially reviewed...
-- UNLESS it's under immigration law.
--
-- Immigration detention is CONSTITUTIONALLY EXEMPT from the
-- habeas corpus requirement of stk. 6.
--
-- Combined with F3 (stk. 1 only covers "dansk borger"):
-- The constitution creates a TWO-TIER LIBERTY SYSTEM:
--   Tier 1: Danish citizens — full § 71 protection
--   Tier 2: Non-citizens — § 71.1 doesn't apply, § 71.6 exempts
--           immigration detention from judicial review
--
-- Our encoding mentions "non-criminal detention" but MISSES the
-- immigration exception entirely. This is our most significant omission.
-- ============================================================================

> udlaendinge_frihedsberoevselse_proeves() -> Bool {
    -- § 71 stk. 6: EXPLICITLY exempt
    False
}

@ print("--- F4: § 71 stk. 6 — immigration detention carve-out ---")
@ print("Text: 'som IKKE har hjemmel i lovgivningen om UDLÆNDINGE'")
@ print("")
@ print("Udlaendinge-frihedsberoevselse proeves: " + show(udlaendinge_frihedsberoevselse_proeves()))
@ print("")
@ print("§ 71 stk. 6 says non-criminal detention gets judicial review")
@ print("EXCEPT immigration detention. The carve-out is in the TEXT.")
@ print("")
@ print("Combined with F3 (stk. 1 = 'dansk borger' only):")
@ print("  TO-LAGS FRIHEDSSYSTEM:")
@ print("    Lag 1: Danske borgere — fuld § 71 beskyttelse")
@ print("    Lag 2: Udlaendinge — stk. 1 gaelder ikke,")
@ print("           stk. 6 undtager udlaendingelov fra proevelse")
@ print("")
@ print("Our encoding: COMPLETELY MISSES this exception.")
@ print("Severity: MENINGSAENDRENDE — the Bill of Rights has a hole")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F5: § 73 stk. 3 vs § 61 — special courts contradiction.
--
-- § 61: "Særdomstole med dømmende myndighed kan IKKE nedsættes."
-- § 73 stk. 3: "Prøvelsen af erstatningens størrelse kan ved lov
--              henlægges til domstole oprettet I DETTE ØJEMED."
--
-- § 61 bans special courts. § 73 allows courts created specifically
-- for expropriation assessment. Is an expropriation court a
-- "særdomstol med dømmende myndighed"?
--
-- If yes: § 73 contradicts § 61.
-- If no: what distinguishes an assessment court from a special court?
--
-- Our encoding doesn't note this tension.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F5: § 73 stk. 3 vs § 61 — special courts contradiction ---")
@ print("§ 61: 'Saerdomstole med doemmende myndighed kan IKKE nedsaettes'")
@ print("§ 73.3: 'domstole oprettet I DETTE OEJEMED' (for ekspropriation)")
@ print("")
@ print("§ 61 forbyder saerdomstole.")
@ print("§ 73.3 tillader domstole oprettet specifikt til ekspropriation.")
@ print("Er en ekspropriationsdomstol en 'saerdomstol'?")
@ print("  Ja → § 73 modsiger § 61")
@ print("  Nej → hvad er forskellen?")
@ print("Severity: STRUKTUREL — self-contradiction in the constitution")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F6: § 77 enumerates three media: "på tryk, i skrift og tale."
--
-- Print, writing, and speech. THREE specific modes.
-- NOT: images, film, video, performance, mime, sculpture, music.
--
-- Our encoding says "ytringsfrihed" (free expression) universally.
-- The text is narrower — it names three modes of publication.
--
-- Is a YouTube video "tale" (speech)? Is a painting "tryk" (print)?
-- Is a mime "skrift" (writing)? Is code "skrift"?
--
-- Modern interpretation extends this to all expression.
-- But the TEXT has an enumeration problem.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F6: § 77 — three modes, not all expression ---")
@ print("Text: 'paa tryk, i skrift og tale'")
@ print("  = in print, in writing, and in speech")
@ print("")
@ print("NOT named: images, film, video, music, art, performance, code")
@ print("Is a YouTube video 'tale'? Is code 'skrift'?")
@ print("Our encoding: 'ytringsfrihed' universally")
@ print("The text: three specific modes from 1849")
@ print("Severity: STRUKTUREL — text is narrower than our encoding")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F7: § 78 stk. 2 — "anderledes tænkende" (those who think differently)
--
-- Text: "strafbar påvirkning af ANDERLEDES TÆNKENDE"
-- Criminal influence on THOSE WHO THINK DIFFERENTLY.
--
-- This is not just anti-violence. It specifically protects DISSENTERS.
-- An association is dissolved not just for using violence generally,
-- but for using violence to influence people who DISAGREE with them.
--
-- Our encoding mentions violence but misses this nuance:
-- § 78.2 protects the freedom to disagree, not just physical safety.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F7: § 78 stk. 2 — 'anderledes taenkende' protection ---")
@ print("Text: 'strafbar paavirkning af ANDERLEDES TAENKENDE'")
@ print("Not just anti-violence — specifically protects DISSENTERS")
@ print("Our encoding: mentions violence, misses the dissenter protection")
@ print("Severity: STRUKTUREL — § 78.2 is about thought-freedom, not just safety")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F8: § 79 "befrygtes fare" — FEARED danger, not actual danger.
--
-- Text: "når der af dem kan BEFRYGTES fare for den offentlige fred"
-- When danger to public peace can be FEARED from them.
--
-- Not "when danger exists" — "when danger can be feared."
-- The threshold is ANTICIPATORY, not factual.
-- Police can ban an outdoor assembly based on what they THINK
-- might happen, not what IS happening.
--
-- Our encoding says "kan forbydes (offentlig fred)" as if the
-- threat must be real. The text allows preventive bans.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F8: § 79 'befrygtes fare' — subjective threat threshold ---")
@ print("Text: 'naar der af dem kan BEFRYGTES fare'")
@ print("Not 'naar fare foreligger' (when danger exists)")
@ print("'Befrygtes' = FEARED. Anticipatory, not factual.")
@ print("Police can ban based on what they THINK might happen.")
@ print("Our encoding: treats threat as objective. Text: subjective.")
@ print("Severity: STRUKTUREL — the ban threshold is lower than we encoded")
@ print("")


-- ============================================================================
-- F9: § 83 abolishes PRIVILEGES, not TITLES.
--
-- Text: "Enhver i lovgivningen til adel, titel og rang knyttet
--  FORRET er afskaffet."
--
-- FORRET (privilege) is what's abolished. Not adel (nobility),
-- not titel (title), not rang (rank) themselves.
-- You can still be "greve" (count) or "baron."
-- The TITLE persists — the legal PRIVILEGE is gone.
--
-- Our encoding says "adelsforrettigheder_eksisterer() -> False"
-- which is correct for privileges but doesn't distinguish from titles.
-- ============================================================================

@ print("--- F9: § 83 — privileges abolished, not titles ---")
@ print("Text: 'til adel, titel og rang knyttet FORRET er afskaffet'")
@ print("FORRET (privilege) is abolished. Not adel/titel/rang themselves.")
@ print("You CAN still be 'greve' or 'baron' — the title is just a word.")
@ print("Denmark has constitutional nobles with no constitutional nobility.")
@ print("Severity: KOSMETISK — our encoding is correct but imprecise")
@ print("")


